    minus over-generic single words. Used as the verbatim-spotting dictionary.

    ``head_aliases`` (default on): also add the distinctive HEAD of compound
    names ("Angiodysplasia of intestine" → "angiodysplasia") so the corpus's
    bare head noun — the form textbooks actually use — is spottable. This closes
    the granularity gap where SNOMED stores site-qualified compounds but the DDx
    prose names only the disease (root-caused angiodysplasia miss, §RESIDUAL_MISS)."""
    vocab: set[str] = set()
    aliases: set[str] = set()
    for c in snomed_concepts.values():
        if c.get("tag") != "disorder":
